    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d126">

                <pb facs="0212" n="96" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg96"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 893.51/415.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State of the
                            American Ambassador to Japan</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Extract.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1911-05-11">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 11, 1911</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Referring to Department’s April 29,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d126-f1"/> in which it
                    was stated that the question of Japanese participation finally rests with the
                    financial groups, it may be added that in case Japan should apply for
                    participation on an equal footing with others not now parties to the London
                    agreement of April 15, the Department would be prepared to support such an
                    application.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Knox</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
